# Git Workflow & KR Alignment

## Branch Naming

Branches should reference the spec or work item:
- `feature/008-sbu-dimension`
- `feature/016-auto-tagging`
- `fix/dashboard-performance`

## Commit Messages

Include parent OKR alignment in commits when meaningful:

```
feat(008): Add SBU filter to initiative list

Alignment: Obj 4 KR3 — reduces time to answer "what are we doing for PBS?"
```

For smaller commits, alignment can be omitted but should be in the PR.

## Pull Requests

PRs MUST include:

1. **Summary** — What changed and why
2. **Parent OKR Alignment** — Which parent objective this advances
3. **Success Metric Impact** — Which PRD 2.4 metric this helps prove

Example PR template:

```markdown
## Summary
[1-2 sentences on what changed]

## Strategic Alignment
- **Parent OKR:** Obj 4 KR3 (Delivery velocity +80%)
- **Success Metric:** Time-to-portfolio-status <30 sec

## Test Plan
- [ ] Verified locally
- [ ] Design principles checklist passed
```

## Before Merging

- [ ] PR has parent OKR alignment documented
- [ ] Code passes linting/tests
- [ ] Design principles checklist reviewed
- [ ] No burden added without burden removed

## Git Practices

- Short-lived branches (1-2 days ideal)
- Atomic commits — one logical change per commit
- Frequent sync with main — rebase before merge
- PR everything — no direct commits to main
